session-import-requirements-local = Use a local session owned by the same user, with an accessible session directory.
herdr-requirements-live = Live migration requires Herdr’s live_handoff capability and shared access to temporary files, sockets, and the ThinkTerm executable.
herdr-requirements-linux = On Linux, /tmp must allow script execution; noexec mounts are unsupported.
session-import-requirements-layout = Saved layouts from stopped sessions need no live handoff. Working directories must exist and ThinkTerm must support the layout format.
session-import-requirements-refresh = Refresh the preview if the session structure or layout changes.
session-import-refresh-preview = Refresh preview
herdr-error-live-unsupported = The running Herdr server does not support live handoff, so its existing processes cannot be moved. Use a Herdr version that supports this capability. Saved layouts from sessions that are not running do not require it.
session-import-error-empty = This session has no terminals to import. Choose another session, or open terminals in { $source } and detect sessions again.
session-import-error-session-missing = The { $source } session directory cannot be accessed. Check that it still exists and is accessible to the current user, then detect sessions again.
session-import-error-directory-missing = One or more saved working directories are missing or inaccessible. Restore them, or update and save the layout in { $source }, then refresh the preview.
session-import-error-layout-newer = This layout format is newer than this version of ThinkTerm supports. Use a ThinkTerm version that supports the format, then refresh the preview.
session-import-error-handoff-version = The live handoff protocol versions are incompatible. Use compatible versions of ThinkTerm and { $source } before trying again.
session-import-error-changed = The session structure, running state, or saved layout changed after the preview. Refresh the preview before confirming the import.
session-import-error-local-user = Use a session owned by the same account on the destination machine. Check its directory and socket permissions.
session-import-error-terminal-missing = Some panes have no live terminal to hand over. The session was not moved. Check those panes in { $source }, then refresh the preview.
session-import-error-receiver = The handoff receiver could not start or connect. Check that both apps can access the same temporary directory, socket, and ThinkTerm executable. On Linux, /tmp must allow script execution (no noexec mount).
session-import-error-inspect = The { $source } session could not be read. Check access to { $source } and its session directories on the target machine, then detect sessions again.
session-import-error-import = The import result could not be confirmed. Check the { $source } session and the destination Space before refreshing the preview or trying again.
session-import-error-open = The session was imported, but its Space could not be opened. Check the target session server connection and retry Open Space. Do not import the session again.
session-import-error-details = Technical details: { $error }
session-import-notes-title = Import notes
session-import-location-local = Import location: this computer
session-import-location-remote = Import location: { $host } · remote processes stay on this server
session-import-requirements-remote = Use a session owned by the remote connection’s account. Terminals and working directories stay on that server.
session-import-hosts = Which machine to import from
session-import-host-local = This computer
session-import-host-connected = Connected
session-import-host-disconnected = Not connected · connects when chosen
session-import-imported = Imported
session-import-already-imported = This session was already imported into { $name }. Importing it again creates another Space.

session-import-check-result = Check import result
session-import-still-running = The import is still running on the target. Check again to retrieve its result.
session-import-result-interrupted = The service was interrupted or the request expired. Its result cannot be confirmed automatically. Check the target Space before starting another import.
session-import-result-unavailable = The connection was interrupted. Check the import result to reconnect and recover this request; do not start a second import.
